WEBVTT

00:03.770 --> 00:07.607
We have seen a star in the east.

00:09.359 --> 00:14.030
It told us
the Son of God is born.

00:46.104 --> 00:49.899
Nativity Play/Sermon/Dinner

00:50.108 --> 00:52.902
The Lord Jesus
was laid in a manger...

00:53.069 --> 00:56.656
...to bring salvation
to the souls of those...

00:56.823 --> 00:59.868
...with no place of their own.

01:00.201 --> 01:03.329
Nothing is harder
than to have no place...

01:03.496 --> 01:07.417
...but many are those
without one.

01:07.667 --> 01:08.877
Tell me about it!

01:09.085 --> 01:12.338
In their solitude,
they long for someone who will say:

01:12.505 --> 01:13.798
"I want you to be here."

01:14.048 --> 01:15.425
Not me, thanks.

01:15.592 --> 01:16.718
Be quiet!

01:17.093 --> 01:22.473
Jesus was born to offer those alone
a place in which to be alive!

01:25.393 --> 01:27.687
"Joy to the world,
the food has come."

01:27.896 --> 01:30.440
Gin! It's "the Lord has come"!

01:31.024 --> 01:32.817
You don't know much, do you?

01:33.026 --> 01:35.528
More than some faggot.

01:35.695 --> 01:38.948
I am a mistake made by God.

01:39.199 --> 01:41.784
In my heart, I am a woman.

01:41.993 --> 01:43.828
Women can have children.

01:44.370 --> 01:47.790
What if a miracle like
the Virgin Mary getting pregnant...

01:47.957 --> 01:50.627
...was to happen to a homo?

01:51.169 --> 01:57.300
Better give me a little extra.
After all, I'm eating for two.

02:21.866 --> 02:23.243
Serves you right!

02:26.371 --> 02:27.455
Miyuki!

02:28.790 --> 02:30.667
Time to eat!

02:34.462 --> 02:35.755
Miyuki!

02:36.130 --> 02:39.342
Close your legs!
Act like you were a woman.

02:39.509 --> 02:40.677
I am a woman.

02:40.844 --> 02:43.721
And it's a waste
to spill food like that.

02:45.223 --> 02:47.433
Don't just gobble your bread.

02:47.600 --> 02:52.272
Eat it with love for the people
who made and brought it here.

02:52.564 --> 02:56.651
I hate that Bible-thumping.
You're just like Akiko.

02:56.943 --> 02:58.319
Who's Akiko?

02:59.988 --> 03:01.072
My old lady.

03:01.239 --> 03:02.031
Well!

03:02.365 --> 03:04.117
Don't call your mother that.

03:04.325 --> 03:06.536
Eat shit, you old fart.

03:06.786 --> 03:09.038
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

03:09.205 --> 03:11.040
That hurts! You old...

03:11.708 --> 03:13.251
..."bag lady."

03:13.501 --> 03:18.464
You peep pretty loud for a chick
that can't even find its own worms.

03:18.631 --> 03:21.968
Should a burden on society
like you be talking?

03:22.135 --> 03:26.139
You're a burden on us.
What does that make you?

03:27.182 --> 03:29.893
The kettle the pot's calling black!

03:31.477 --> 03:33.104
You mouthy brat!

03:33.980 --> 03:37.483
Can't you at least get along
at Christmas?

03:38.067 --> 03:41.112
Oh, yes...
Miyuki, I got you a present.

03:44.365 --> 03:45.783
They're gone!

03:45.950 --> 03:49.162
A whole set of
"World Literature for Children."

03:49.329 --> 03:51.748
Why would I need that?!

03:51.915 --> 03:53.666
Hana looked hard for those!

03:53.875 --> 03:57.879
Even a homeless teenage runaway
needs a Christmas present!

03:59.297 --> 04:01.382
I choose not to go home.

04:01.591 --> 04:05.011
Six months on the street
means you don't have a home.

04:05.220 --> 04:07.931
I can go home
any time I want to.

04:08.223 --> 04:11.684
It's the ones who say that
who never do.

04:11.893 --> 04:13.937
Speak for yourself,
you old geezer!

04:14.437 --> 04:17.273
What are you doing
to Dostoevsky?!

04:18.191 --> 04:21.653
I won't take that,
today of all days!

04:22.904 --> 04:26.115
Not even my father
ever hit me!

04:27.325 --> 04:29.953
So I'll do it for him!

04:33.790 --> 04:36.292
Grow up, will you?!

04:37.585 --> 04:38.795
Don't hurt yourselves.

04:39.587 --> 04:41.214
Show more respect, kid!

04:41.422 --> 04:42.966
I'm not a kid!

04:43.132 --> 04:45.635
With little tits like these?

04:45.802 --> 04:47.887
You filthy old pervert!
That's harassment!

04:48.137 --> 04:50.056
Will you two stop!

04:53.184 --> 04:54.060
Huh?

05:13.621 --> 05:15.039
It's been...

05:15.290 --> 05:16.583
...abandoned.

05:17.292 --> 05:19.294
There, there, there.

05:22.297 --> 05:24.424
Care for this child.

05:26.885 --> 05:28.595
What a world!

05:29.304 --> 05:30.013
Oh, man!

05:30.180 --> 05:34.601
Oh, my! You're a little girl.
I wonder what your name is.

05:34.767 --> 05:36.394
"John Doe."

05:36.561 --> 05:38.730
She's a girl, I said!
He's so rude!

05:39.564 --> 05:45.111
How old was I when I started
living like this? Thirty-something?

05:47.113 --> 05:51.075
I still thought
that I was better off...

05:51.868 --> 05:53.745
...than a child with no home.

06:01.461 --> 06:05.798
There, there, now! We'll take you
somewhere warm.

06:08.218 --> 06:10.720
The cop shop's that way!

06:12.514 --> 06:15.058
This is a Christmas present
from God!

06:15.225 --> 06:17.894
She's our baby!

06:18.186 --> 06:19.062
Huh?

06:30.281 --> 06:33.743
A Tokyo Godfathers Committee
Production

06:37.163 --> 06:40.625
Developed by Masao Maruyama
Original Story by Satoshi Kon

06:41.543 --> 06:45.004
Screenplay by
Keiko Nobumoto and Satoshi Kon

06:47.173 --> 06:50.635
Character Design
Kenichi Konishi and Satoshi Kon

06:50.802 --> 06:54.264
Animation Director
Kenichi Konishi

06:55.181 --> 06:58.643
Art Director Nobutaka Ike
Color Design Satoshi Hashimoto

06:58.810 --> 07:00.103
Co-Director Shogo Furuya

07:00.270 --> 07:02.272
Director of Photography
Katsutoshi Sugai

07:04.190 --> 07:07.652
Music by Keiichi Suzuki
Sound Director Masafumi Mima

07:09.737 --> 07:11.114
Sorry!

07:11.531 --> 07:14.450
What do you mean,
take her with us?

07:14.742 --> 07:17.203
I'm just doing God's will.

07:17.495 --> 07:19.372
Her parents might come back.

07:19.706 --> 07:23.126
What parent would leave
a child out in this cold?!

07:23.334 --> 07:26.004
That's a devil, not a parent!

07:28.923 --> 07:32.302
Kiyoko wanted us
to find her.

07:32.468 --> 07:33.595
"Kiyoko"?

07:33.803 --> 07:36.306
"Kiyoko"? Why "Kiyoko"?!

07:36.764 --> 07:40.643
From kiyo, "pure",
on this purest of nights.

07:41.269 --> 07:42.145
How tacky!

07:42.312 --> 07:44.480
Kiyoko's a fine name!

07:44.647 --> 07:46.983
Did you have
a girlfriend named that?

07:47.150 --> 07:48.484
Idiot!

07:48.860 --> 07:53.656
Look, we can't just name her!
She's not a puppy or a kitten!

07:53.823 --> 07:55.325
So I'm taking her home.

07:55.491 --> 07:56.826
To a cardboard box?

07:56.993 --> 07:58.661
There's no room!

07:58.912 --> 08:04.000
This is a once-in-a-lifetime chance!
Let me feel like a mother!

08:07.128 --> 08:08.713
A haiku:

08:09.339 --> 08:15.595
"A little baby / powdery snow
on its cheeks / on this holy night."

08:15.762 --> 08:19.682
Directed by
Satoshi Kon

08:31.653 --> 08:33.279
Peek-a-boo!

08:35.240 --> 08:37.534
Oh, dear! Tell me what's wrong!

08:37.700 --> 08:39.285
Shut up!

08:43.540 --> 08:44.123
Hey!

08:44.332 --> 08:48.920
I know, I know, he's not your mommy.
He's just a homeless homo.

08:49.212 --> 08:51.798
Don't say that
in front of her!

08:52.006 --> 08:55.677
A baby crying around here
will sound weird!

08:56.010 --> 08:59.138
We're going to take you
to the police soon, okay?

08:59.347 --> 09:01.683
You're not going anywhere,
are you?

09:01.891 --> 09:04.519
Idiot! We're taking
her to the police!

09:04.727 --> 09:06.813
Don't shout
or she'll never shut up!

09:07.021 --> 09:10.400
Why won't you stop crying?
Are you hungry?

09:10.567 --> 09:11.484
There, there!

09:11.693 --> 09:14.112
Maybe she's sick.

09:27.834 --> 09:31.504
Tomorrow...
I promise I'll take her then.

09:32.672 --> 09:37.177
Christmas should be
the happiest day of the year.

09:37.385 --> 09:40.763
If we take her in now, it'll always be
the worst day of her life!

09:42.473 --> 09:43.558
Maybe...

09:44.309 --> 09:46.186
...she needs a diaper.

09:56.196 --> 09:57.780
Hana, boil some water.

09:58.239 --> 09:59.616
I'll make some milk.

09:59.908 --> 10:02.160
Hey! Whose side are you on?!

10:02.368 --> 10:06.789
Go buy some water!
My angel isn't drinking from the tap!

10:07.123 --> 10:08.791
Why me?

10:10.293 --> 10:14.797
Where does a bum get off telling me
"Them that works eats"?

10:16.674 --> 10:21.554
Just for tonight, remember.
Tomorrow we take her to the police.

10:23.932 --> 10:27.936
So "no man is an island"
after all, huh?

10:32.106 --> 10:34.192
You're buying water?!

10:35.109 --> 10:37.070
A Christmas miracle.

10:37.612 --> 10:39.697
What a haul!

10:46.287 --> 10:48.498
Watch where you're going, brat!

10:48.665 --> 10:50.500
You watch where you're going!

10:54.003 --> 10:56.631
I was married once.

10:56.965 --> 10:58.424
With a child?

10:58.591 --> 11:02.512
No, don't tell me!
I don't want to hear this!

11:04.097 --> 11:07.350
You never forget
for one second.

11:07.517 --> 11:11.938
A child's the only thing
you hold dearer than life itself.

11:13.439 --> 11:14.732
A boy?

11:15.191 --> 11:16.442
No.

11:20.947 --> 11:22.282
Bullshit!

11:22.448 --> 11:24.450
Come on! Give it back!

11:24.784 --> 11:29.038
Hey, you're the girl
who hangs out with Gin.

11:29.247 --> 11:30.874
Get out of here, will you?

11:31.040 --> 11:33.585
We don't want Gin after us.

11:34.919 --> 11:35.545
Why not?

11:35.712 --> 11:39.132
You're the light of his life,
that's why not!

11:39.674 --> 11:44.804
There's not much light
in a cardboard box.

11:45.096 --> 11:47.265
Let me have this book.

11:49.893 --> 11:51.811
How old?

11:51.978 --> 11:54.230
Twenty-one, I think.

11:54.689 --> 11:58.818
Five or six years older
than Miyuki, I guess.

11:59.027 --> 12:00.820
That old?

12:00.987 --> 12:03.406
If she was alive.

12:05.033 --> 12:09.621
When I was 20 I got a girl pregnant,
and we got married.

12:10.079 --> 12:12.123
I was in heaven.

12:12.498 --> 12:16.336
You could have poked me in the eye
and I'd have just smiled at you.

12:16.544 --> 12:22.425
But my daughter got sick,
and the medical bills were huge.

12:22.634 --> 12:27.263
I was something of
a bicycle racer then.

12:27.889 --> 12:31.518
I needed money.
There was this race...

12:31.726 --> 12:32.936
You threw it?

12:35.396 --> 12:39.234
A punk I knew
had this scheme.

12:39.400 --> 12:45.281
They found out, I got kicked out
of racing, and my girl died.

12:45.573 --> 12:48.701
I just didn't feel
like working anymore.

12:48.910 --> 12:52.038
And then my wife
followed my daughter.

12:52.205 --> 12:53.289
Oh, no!

12:54.666 --> 12:57.168
That's how you get to be
a man like me.

12:57.460 --> 13:00.880
I didn't want to hear that!
I hate sad stories!

13:02.131 --> 13:04.259
It's freezing!

13:07.887 --> 13:09.138
You're used to this.

13:09.305 --> 13:10.515
Kind of.

13:10.682 --> 13:13.393
I'll give her the milk.

13:14.435 --> 13:16.229
Dreams do come true.

13:16.396 --> 13:21.150
I always dreamed of being
the mother of a little girl.

13:21.317 --> 13:23.570
A nice, warm house,
a pretty daughter.

13:23.778 --> 13:26.406
Even if my husband
was no good...

13:26.614 --> 13:29.576
...I would accept dire poverty
as long as I had my child.

13:29.742 --> 13:31.786
Feed the poor kid!

13:36.791 --> 13:38.668
You're so pretty.

13:39.460 --> 13:43.214
The prettiest little girl
in the world.

14:08.531 --> 14:09.741
What do you want?!

14:10.241 --> 14:11.534
They're gone.

14:14.829 --> 14:16.956
Santa Claus, maybe?

14:17.207 --> 14:20.293
"Uncle Bag" and the baby
are gone.

14:20.460 --> 14:23.254
What's that faggot
thinking about?!

14:26.049 --> 14:28.551
Man, he's got big feet!

14:28.718 --> 14:31.054
You can't have feet fixed.

14:48.112 --> 14:49.989
Are you taking her back?

14:51.407 --> 14:53.826
There's probably an APB
out on her.

14:54.202 --> 14:55.745
And for you.

14:55.912 --> 14:56.663
I doubt it.

14:57.705 --> 15:01.000
An arrest warrant, maybe.

15:02.377 --> 15:05.505
Her parents are probably
sorry about this now.

15:05.755 --> 15:08.049
So let's take her to the police.

15:08.800 --> 15:13.012
A baby's always
better off with its real mother.

15:13.221 --> 15:15.014
Not necessarily.

15:16.891 --> 15:19.477
Sometimes a
foster mother's better.

15:19.686 --> 15:22.021
- What?!
- Don't be stupid.

15:22.814 --> 15:26.025
I never knew
my real mother.

15:28.027 --> 15:32.657
But I'll bet if she saw me now,
she'd flip.

15:33.992 --> 15:36.870
How can someone homeless
raise a child?

15:37.036 --> 15:39.539
I know, I know!

15:40.582 --> 15:44.294
I don't want her shunted
from one foster home to another...

15:44.586 --> 15:46.754
...without even one memory...

15:46.963 --> 15:49.174
...of ever having been loved.

15:49.507 --> 15:52.886
You don't have to be a foundling
to feel that.

15:53.386 --> 15:55.555
They must have had reasons.

15:55.763 --> 15:58.558
Nothing should make you
abandon a child!

16:00.143 --> 16:05.148
That means you've taken love
and tossed it away, like trash.

16:06.608 --> 16:09.569
Yeah, but what can we
do about it?

16:10.278 --> 16:11.696
Find her mother.

16:13.907 --> 16:16.951
And ask why she abandoned
her baby.

16:18.328 --> 16:20.788
If she can make me understand...

16:21.664 --> 16:24.292
...I'll forgive her,
and my mother too.

16:25.126 --> 16:27.212
Find her?

16:27.420 --> 16:29.047
How?

16:33.134 --> 16:35.094
We'll have to pay again.

16:35.637 --> 16:38.765
This is an expensive year-end!

16:39.098 --> 16:41.226
What if we find another baby?

16:41.392 --> 16:43.937
They don't toss them out in twos.

16:55.156 --> 16:56.950
Another key!

16:57.158 --> 17:01.120
Look at these panties.
You'd catch cold in them!

17:01.788 --> 17:04.332
Are they the ones?

17:07.836 --> 17:09.879
Are these your folks?

17:10.380 --> 17:12.215
Look, business cards.

17:19.681 --> 17:23.142
A hostess club
won't be open at this hour!

17:23.601 --> 17:25.979
We've got some walking to do.

17:26.145 --> 17:28.398
You've gotta be kidding!

17:31.693 --> 17:33.653
He was eating for two!

17:46.875 --> 17:52.505
But why pack like you're off on a trip
and then abandon a baby?

17:53.047 --> 17:56.301
Maybe it was one last trip
they were taking.

17:56.467 --> 17:57.635
A family suicide?!

17:59.262 --> 18:00.597
Then what do we do?

18:01.097 --> 18:03.224
We can't search the next world!

18:03.433 --> 18:04.893
Shh!

18:11.024 --> 18:14.068
We apologize for
any inconvenience.

18:14.235 --> 18:18.823
Trains will be delayed due
to heavy snowfall.

18:19.574 --> 18:21.075
It's so hot in here!

18:21.284 --> 18:22.994
What a stink!

18:23.620 --> 18:26.539
Have you bathed lately?

18:27.248 --> 18:29.125
No. Or washed my clothes.

18:29.292 --> 18:31.002
How embarrassing!

18:40.970 --> 18:42.931
Oh, dear! There, there.

18:43.097 --> 18:46.434
Did she piss herself?
That's why it stinks!

18:46.601 --> 18:48.311
It's you that stinks!

18:48.561 --> 18:49.521
Quiet!

18:49.729 --> 18:51.564
Shut that kid up!

19:06.246 --> 19:07.539
Watch it!

19:08.414 --> 19:09.123
Hey!

19:18.508 --> 19:19.717
Miyuki!

19:19.926 --> 19:21.553
What's she up to?

19:28.142 --> 19:30.562
We wasted our train fares!

19:31.145 --> 19:33.481
It was me who paid them.

19:34.941 --> 19:38.570
I'm sorry!
There's no more milk.

19:38.820 --> 19:41.155
Go ahead, blame it all on me.

19:41.364 --> 19:44.534
Oh, cheer up!
Let's sing a song.

19:49.455 --> 19:50.415
What's that?

19:50.582 --> 19:52.166
The Sound of Music,
of course.

19:52.375 --> 19:53.376
Never heard of it.

20:01.634 --> 20:04.971
That's going to make you
even hungrier.

20:14.063 --> 20:15.815
I'm starving!

20:16.482 --> 20:18.443
I told you!

20:18.902 --> 20:21.446
Look after my little angel.

20:22.780 --> 20:24.324
Go on without me.

20:24.657 --> 20:28.953
Just say you'll never forget
the queer you once knew.

20:29.412 --> 20:31.789
Look.
A cemetery.

20:31.956 --> 20:33.875
I'm not dead yet!

20:46.721 --> 20:49.599
Now I'm alive again!

20:50.683 --> 20:55.563
But there's nothing for a baby
in these offerings to the dead!

20:55.730 --> 20:57.732
We'll get by!

20:58.191 --> 21:00.818
Yeah, sure! "We'll get by!"

21:01.027 --> 21:04.197
People keep on saying that
till they end up living like us!

21:04.531 --> 21:10.203
And while we keep on saying it,
the kid'll end up under a stone here.

21:10.370 --> 21:12.080
"Kiyoko"! She has a name!

21:12.247 --> 21:17.085
Yeah, whatever. And she's cute.
She's so pretty.

21:17.502 --> 21:20.088
But listen to me. I'm serious.

21:20.630 --> 21:21.840
You listening?

21:23.049 --> 21:26.511
If you really care
about that kid...

21:26.719 --> 21:29.764
...you'll find her someone
to take care of her.

21:29.973 --> 21:32.350
I speak from experience.

21:32.600 --> 21:34.727
That's what her parents said, I bet.

21:34.894 --> 21:38.523
What do you mean?
I wouldn't abandon a kid.

21:38.815 --> 21:41.067
Don't be stupid!

21:41.234 --> 21:44.195
No. Your family
abandoned you!

21:44.779 --> 21:48.199
There you go again!
Am I going to sit and listen...

21:48.408 --> 21:51.327
...while some dumb faggot
pisses on me?

21:51.494 --> 21:55.456
What are we doing here?
Tell me.

21:55.665 --> 21:57.500
Wracking our brains!

21:57.667 --> 22:00.962
We're scavenging offerings
left in a cemetery.

22:01.129 --> 22:03.923
And why? Because
we're homeless.

22:04.215 --> 22:07.093
- Stop it!
- No! I'm not going to stop.

22:07.343 --> 22:10.221
We are three
good-for-nothing bums...

22:10.430 --> 22:12.807
...who can't even
look after ourselves.

22:13.057 --> 22:15.143
Shut up! I'm thinking!

22:15.518 --> 22:17.270
I won't shut up.

22:17.520 --> 22:22.650
You can't get milk from an old queer's
tits, no matter how hard you think.

22:22.942 --> 22:27.238
Come on, Hana! You know
we can't do this.

22:27.530 --> 22:29.073
Speak for yourself!

22:29.490 --> 22:32.452
This way the whole family
will be dead.

22:41.294 --> 22:43.129
Oh, my!

22:44.339 --> 22:46.799
You're so lucky, Kiyoko!

22:46.966 --> 22:49.135
God must really love you!

22:50.178 --> 22:51.596
Then why was she...

22:51.763 --> 22:53.139
...dumped?

22:54.182 --> 22:55.642
Left!

22:55.808 --> 22:59.812
- That's a dead end!
- It's right!

23:02.732 --> 23:04.609
- Tails.
- Heads.

23:13.701 --> 23:16.704
What's this guy doing
parking like that?

23:16.871 --> 23:19.999
Doesn't he know what
a "public thoroughfare" is?

23:40.603 --> 23:42.146
How did that happen?

23:42.355 --> 23:48.278
Bad luck. The car got stuck,
and I forgot the parking brake.

23:48.444 --> 23:50.655
Then someone shouted,
"Dorothy, wait!"...

23:50.864 --> 23:52.657
...and then I heard, "Whoops!"...

23:53.199 --> 23:56.786
...and the damn car
rolled on top of me.

23:58.037 --> 24:04.043
I don't bring my men with me
when I'm visiting the old man's grave.

24:04.586 --> 24:08.339
I owe you. Call me
if you're ever in trouble.

24:08.590 --> 24:10.758
Oh, no, we never have
any trouble.

24:10.967 --> 24:13.011
You're from Kinshicho?

24:13.178 --> 24:15.847
We were just going there.

24:16.014 --> 24:18.308
I know it's rude to ask...

24:18.474 --> 24:20.518
If it's rude, then don't ask.

24:20.727 --> 24:22.187
Come on.

24:23.563 --> 24:26.357
Would you know
this establishment?

24:26.566 --> 24:27.901
Club Swirl: "Midori"

24:29.110 --> 24:30.778
Know it?

24:31.613 --> 24:35.783
Its owner's marrying
my daughter today.

24:37.118 --> 24:41.873
He's one of my men,
but he's too cocky.

24:42.081 --> 24:44.417
I was against it.

24:44.584 --> 24:46.753
But your daughter chose him.

24:47.086 --> 24:50.757
The daughter I brought up,
married to a man like that...

24:52.342 --> 24:53.468
Know what I mean?

24:54.344 --> 24:58.681
But if your daughter's
happy with him...

24:58.848 --> 25:00.725
...isn't that the main thing?

25:00.892 --> 25:01.893
You're right!

25:02.101 --> 25:09.108
I went to the old man's grave
so I wouldn't cry at the wedding.

25:09.359 --> 25:11.110
Watch the road!

25:16.783 --> 25:18.326
Good evening, sir!

25:20.370 --> 25:22.288
Make yourselves at home.

25:35.301 --> 25:37.011
Daddy, you're late!

25:37.220 --> 25:41.099
Sorry, sorry.
I almost got killed.

25:41.266 --> 25:44.227
I owe them my life.

25:44.394 --> 25:45.895
My daughter, Kiyoko.

25:46.062 --> 25:47.313
Oh. Hello.

25:57.866 --> 26:00.743
What have you gotten us into?!

26:00.910 --> 26:03.204
Just shut up and eat!

26:06.833 --> 26:09.586
Diaper change.
Your turn, Miyuki.

26:17.927 --> 26:22.265
Don't you think Kiyoko
has amazing luck?

26:24.767 --> 26:25.810
Yeah.

26:26.519 --> 26:28.479
Maybe she does.

26:31.941 --> 26:34.652
Oh, yeah. Her name's Sachiko.

26:35.195 --> 26:36.487
Not "Midori"?

26:36.654 --> 26:38.198
Just at the club.

26:38.364 --> 26:41.159
She's Sachiko, "happy child,"
though she didn't look it.

26:41.326 --> 26:46.331
But some plastic surgery
turned her into a good little earner.

26:47.957 --> 26:50.668
She quit.
Said she was pregnant.

26:50.877 --> 26:52.837
Do you know where she is?

26:53.713 --> 26:56.257
I doubt you'll wring
any money out of her.

26:56.966 --> 26:59.761
No, I have something
to give her.

27:03.598 --> 27:07.060
I'm sorry
I spilled your food.

27:07.435 --> 27:10.688
You remember her?
Midori, the skinny broad.

27:12.565 --> 27:14.692
She said her husband
was in debt.

27:14.859 --> 27:16.945
What's wrong with you?

27:17.111 --> 27:18.363
That bastard.

27:18.571 --> 27:20.740
Do you know him?

27:21.324 --> 27:23.201
Then she borrowed
more money from us...

27:23.493 --> 27:26.496
...and ended up screwed both ways.

27:26.788 --> 27:28.748
You know where she is?

27:29.624 --> 27:30.291
If it weren't for his
damn get-rich-quick scheme...

27:30.291 --> 27:33.127
If it weren't for his
damn get-rich-quick scheme...

27:33.294 --> 27:36.047
...l'd still be with
my wife and kid!

27:36.256 --> 27:38.800
But aren't they both dead?

27:38.967 --> 27:41.135
I'll kill the bastard!

27:42.178 --> 27:44.305
You'll get killed!

28:11.207 --> 28:12.542
Mitsuo! Mitsuo!

28:12.709 --> 28:15.003
It was that maid!

28:15.170 --> 28:17.046
Are you okay?!

28:18.131 --> 28:19.465
She's got a gun!

28:21.134 --> 28:22.177
Hey, what?!

28:27.182 --> 28:29.017
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

28:30.143 --> 28:31.102
Hey!

28:53.041 --> 28:55.835
Thank you very much.

28:56.669 --> 28:59.047
She's got a gun, you know!

28:59.214 --> 29:02.675
- Our lives are already wasted!
- Hana!

29:08.348 --> 29:09.057
There!

29:34.624 --> 29:38.962
Yes! One of your cabs picked up
a young woman with a baby.

29:39.128 --> 29:42.048
Number 12-25. Send it to...

29:43.216 --> 29:46.135
...the Tokyo Tower.
My name is

29:48.555 --> 29:51.266
Hey! Wait a minute.

29:55.395 --> 30:00.275
We're homeless bums,
not action-movie heroes.

30:00.733 --> 30:02.735
What we need now
is the police.

30:03.778 --> 30:08.700
If you like the police so much,
get them to adopt you!

30:08.867 --> 30:11.578
Those children are like family!

30:11.744 --> 30:13.746
I thought I could
depend on you!

30:14.080 --> 30:17.458
Don't talk like you were
my damn wife.

30:19.752 --> 30:21.296
I'm not going anywhere.

30:21.504 --> 30:22.630
Gin!

30:23.131 --> 30:25.216
We've done all we could.

30:25.425 --> 30:26.551
You're giving up?

30:27.594 --> 30:30.388
There's nothing we can do.

30:30.930 --> 30:33.600
You are really
the lowest of the low!

30:33.766 --> 30:36.895
The best thing you'll ever do
is die in the gutter!

30:37.061 --> 30:40.732
Oh, poor you! You'll be dead
and no one'll care!

30:40.940 --> 30:43.818
All you ever do is
cause people trouble!

30:43.985 --> 30:46.571
Dead or alive, you're living trash!

30:46.738 --> 30:49.449
The king of trash!

30:53.620 --> 30:57.999
Okay, so I'm trash.
But you're ugly.

31:13.723 --> 31:17.477
- Yes?
- I want to get rid of some trash.

31:22.815 --> 31:25.235
I don't think I'd fit.

31:26.069 --> 31:30.990
Yeah, that's what I am,
living trash!

31:32.575 --> 31:36.829
Who cares if you die
in the gutter?

31:38.081 --> 31:41.668
You're dead all the same.

32:03.857 --> 32:05.817
You okay?

32:06.609 --> 32:08.945
Hang in there, Gramps.

32:11.406 --> 32:14.742
- May I make one last request?
- What?

32:16.578 --> 32:18.746
Give me a drink of that.

33:09.464 --> 33:12.091
You're not selling me
into slavery!

33:14.093 --> 33:16.221
Somebody, help!

33:30.443 --> 33:34.572
I always wanted to die drunk,
in a nice old house.

33:34.739 --> 33:37.784
Now I'm halfway there.

33:38.034 --> 33:40.161
Fate works in strange ways.

33:41.162 --> 33:43.957
L've lived a long time...

33:44.123 --> 33:47.710
...but I'm just trash,
as worthless dead as alive.

33:48.044 --> 33:50.171
Don't talk like that!

33:51.005 --> 33:55.176
You remind me of myself
when I was younger.

33:55.718 --> 33:58.179
Looking at you now...

33:58.555 --> 34:01.683
...may I make a last request?

34:02.392 --> 34:05.270
Get rid of this for me.

34:05.562 --> 34:11.192
Some people will be hurt
if it's known who I am.

34:11.401 --> 34:15.029
Okay. I understand.
No one will ever know.

34:28.918 --> 34:33.256
Take care of yourself, okay?
May I make a last...?

34:34.048 --> 34:35.216
Request?

34:40.930 --> 34:43.641
And now, goodbye.

34:58.948 --> 35:00.033
That's it!

35:03.203 --> 35:04.996
Thanks, Gramps!

35:10.752 --> 35:13.588
Time for the New Year's clean-up!

35:21.930 --> 35:23.806
Big breasts... Cool!

35:36.486 --> 35:38.863
Husband?

35:53.837 --> 35:55.088
Father

35:55.922 --> 35:56.923
Police.

35:57.090 --> 35:58.925
Your dad's a cop?!

35:59.175 --> 36:00.635
My father was a policeman!

36:01.052 --> 36:02.512
Father, policeman?

36:05.014 --> 36:10.520
Except I'm the one
he's going to be arresting.

36:25.285 --> 36:26.494
Hold it.

36:29.789 --> 36:32.125
Hi! How've you been?

36:34.711 --> 36:36.546
Now? Just cleaning up.

36:36.838 --> 36:39.007
Hey, wake up!

36:39.174 --> 36:40.258
Come on!

36:43.720 --> 36:45.763
No! Not that!

36:47.015 --> 36:48.683
Time to die, old man!

36:48.850 --> 36:52.020
Kiyo's coming? I'm there!

36:52.687 --> 36:54.856
The girls are drinking near here.

36:55.064 --> 36:56.608
Yeah?

36:58.026 --> 37:00.028
All cleaned up.

37:04.407 --> 37:05.617
Give it back!

37:06.910 --> 37:09.120
Give me that back!

37:10.580 --> 37:15.335
Her foreigner husband looked like
he was in a real bad mood.

37:16.085 --> 37:17.295
Did he hit her?

37:17.462 --> 37:20.798
No, she was being real nice
for a girl so young.

37:21.007 --> 37:24.219
My wife could learn something!

37:25.220 --> 37:28.640
His foreign assailant fled, taking
a young woman and a baby hostage.

37:28.806 --> 37:33.686
With the groom in serious condition,
police speculate this may be a war...

37:34.020 --> 37:36.231
...between crime syndicates.

37:36.689 --> 37:39.526
Hey, this is serious!

37:39.692 --> 37:41.736
I'm not kidding around, either!

37:48.409 --> 37:50.286
My mom's religious.

37:50.453 --> 37:52.580
She chants all the time.

37:58.628 --> 37:59.629
Me.

38:04.217 --> 38:05.802
Isn't she cute?

38:06.219 --> 38:09.514
I found her. Those spots
on her back look like wings.

38:09.681 --> 38:11.307
So I called her "Angel."

38:13.059 --> 38:15.228
But she's gone.

38:18.314 --> 38:19.524
Father.

38:30.201 --> 38:32.078
I stabbed my father.

38:32.537 --> 38:34.831
I can never go back.

39:01.316 --> 39:04.110
The baby? A gift from God.

39:04.277 --> 39:05.153
Yes.

39:06.279 --> 39:08.698
Give me a break!

39:08.948 --> 39:10.783
L've got a family at home!

39:10.950 --> 39:13.369
Those children are my family!

39:14.996 --> 39:16.664
They went in there.

39:17.332 --> 39:18.208
Hey! The fare!

39:18.374 --> 39:19.667
I'll be right back.

39:19.959 --> 39:22.212
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

39:23.505 --> 39:25.465
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

39:25.632 --> 39:27.300
Where are you?

39:34.516 --> 39:37.393
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

39:54.160 --> 39:56.621
How could you do this to me?!

39:58.206 --> 39:59.582
It's your own fault!

40:00.458 --> 40:03.503
You never listen
to anything I say!

40:03.670 --> 40:05.713
Use the scarf I made you...

40:05.922 --> 40:07.674
...to mop up the blood!

40:07.841 --> 40:09.217
What have you done
with Angel?!

40:09.425 --> 40:12.136
Where is she?
Where is my Angel?

40:12.762 --> 40:14.180
She's right here.

40:14.472 --> 40:15.890
Our angel.

40:18.184 --> 40:19.936
I'm hungry.

40:20.186 --> 40:21.604
Make me some food.

40:22.856 --> 40:23.690
Why?

40:24.315 --> 40:26.609
What are you doing in my house?

40:26.776 --> 40:30.947
Miyuki, take Kiyoko.
I'll get dinner.

40:41.332 --> 40:46.129
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

40:51.134 --> 40:52.468
Uncle Bag?!

40:56.306 --> 40:59.893
Oh, I've missed you,
my little angel!

41:03.646 --> 41:07.400
I wish I was her mother,
but I'm just another homo.

41:08.735 --> 41:09.527
Miyuki...

41:11.112 --> 41:12.864
...I'm so glad you're safe.

41:22.248 --> 41:23.041
Where's the geezer?

41:24.042 --> 41:26.544
He could be dead
for all I care!

41:29.172 --> 41:31.674
I'm dying.

41:41.518 --> 41:43.895
Maybe he went home.

41:44.062 --> 41:45.313
Who cares?

41:45.688 --> 41:47.982
All he thinks about
is himself.

41:49.400 --> 41:54.155
Yeah, Miss Hana, but you're
in love with him, aren't you?

41:54.364 --> 41:58.243
Don't be silly! I like my men
to be more "manly."

41:58.409 --> 42:03.873
The kind of man I like is
slender, middle-aged, tanned...

42:04.040 --> 42:07.502
...with a divine square-back haircut
and a lower-town accent...

42:07.710 --> 42:10.713
...who says, "Ah, what the hell"...

42:10.880 --> 42:14.092
...when I don't quite have
the cab fare.

42:17.387 --> 42:19.806
So, what now, Miss Hana?

42:19.973 --> 42:24.185
Why are you calling me that?
"Uncle Bag" is fine.

42:24.394 --> 42:26.563
It's hard to say.

42:33.611 --> 42:35.071
I'm glad.

42:38.116 --> 42:39.200
He just died there?

42:39.409 --> 42:40.785
He was homeless.

42:40.952 --> 42:42.412
I might be next.

42:42.579 --> 42:43.746
Just do your job.

42:43.913 --> 42:45.957
Gin!

42:48.668 --> 42:51.087
Gin! Gin!

42:51.754 --> 42:53.298
Take it easy.

42:53.464 --> 42:54.424
Gin!

42:54.591 --> 42:56.134
Calm down!

43:04.642 --> 43:08.354
Where is that man of mine?!

43:09.480 --> 43:14.068
Kiyo...

43:15.111 --> 43:19.741
If only tonight...

43:21.159 --> 43:25.371
...I wanted to see you
before I died.

43:27.957 --> 43:30.585
Kiyoko!

43:46.267 --> 43:49.979
What is your desire?
My magic, or an ambulance?

43:50.939 --> 43:53.983
- An ambulance.
- Well! Aren't you rude!

43:55.193 --> 43:59.489
What are we going to do?
Kiyoko can't sleep out on the street!

43:59.656 --> 44:03.785
The geezer's not here,
we're freezing, sleepy, hungry.

44:03.993 --> 44:05.495
This sucks!

44:06.162 --> 44:08.790
I guess there's no choice.

44:14.546 --> 44:17.090
I never thought
I'd be here again.

44:23.346 --> 44:27.684
I'm sorry. We're closed for
a private party tonight

44:29.853 --> 44:31.145
Hana?!

44:31.563 --> 44:35.567
I know I have no right
to come strolling in now...

44:35.733 --> 44:39.612
...but there's no one else
I can call on, "Mother"!

44:44.242 --> 44:45.827
Hana!

44:46.578 --> 44:47.829
Mother!

44:48.037 --> 44:49.372
Hana!

44:57.088 --> 44:58.047
Geezer?!

45:01.342 --> 45:03.219
What happened, Gin?!

45:05.597 --> 45:08.183
Some kids beat me up.

45:09.142 --> 45:12.103
I guess I'm just not
an action hero.

45:16.482 --> 45:19.110
He said he knew you.

45:19.444 --> 45:22.530
But he said he was homeless,
you know.

45:23.573 --> 45:24.949
So am I.

45:25.116 --> 45:28.786
What? But why?!

45:30.079 --> 45:32.332
Since Ken died I'm like a canary...

45:32.498 --> 45:34.792
...that's forgotten its song.

45:35.251 --> 45:37.504
You sing all the time!

45:38.880 --> 45:40.256
Isn't she cute?!

45:40.423 --> 45:42.008
I wish I could have one!

45:47.388 --> 45:50.892
So Ken died, did he?

45:53.102 --> 45:54.354
AIDS?

45:55.063 --> 45:57.273
He slipped on the soap.

45:57.440 --> 46:01.402
Well, death is always
a hair's breadth away.

46:01.945 --> 46:06.032
But if you were in trouble,
why didn't you come back?

46:08.785 --> 46:12.205
We certainly had fun here,
didn't we?

46:13.998 --> 46:16.459
In this old bar

46:16.709 --> 46:20.255
I've had so much to drink

46:21.172 --> 46:23.258
My old memories

46:23.883 --> 46:28.221
All start to blur

46:28.471 --> 46:30.890
My lover

46:31.057 --> 46:34.352
Has left me

46:35.645 --> 46:40.817
People call me notorious

46:40.984 --> 46:42.819
Aw, you're ugly!

46:43.319 --> 46:45.738
Good for nothing

46:45.905 --> 46:46.739
Get off!

46:46.906 --> 46:49.617
Good for nothing

46:50.618 --> 46:54.289
What a terrible thing to say

46:54.497 --> 46:56.916
Eat shit, you old fart!

46:58.543 --> 47:02.630
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

47:09.637 --> 47:12.807
I couldn't come back
after I'd done that.

47:13.224 --> 47:17.103
A little bit of money
took care of that.

47:17.270 --> 47:20.064
I'm just happy you're all right.

47:22.233 --> 47:25.945
Stop it! You scare me
when you start crying.

47:27.697 --> 47:31.868
What about that baby?
Is the girl its mother?

47:32.035 --> 47:33.286
Well...

47:36.706 --> 47:40.210
Where is your mother, anyway?

47:41.252 --> 47:42.378
Abandoned?!

47:42.545 --> 47:45.965
Yes! L've been abandoned!

47:48.468 --> 47:51.137
Them's the breaks, I guess.

47:52.555 --> 47:55.058
I could see me in her.

47:55.308 --> 47:59.521
Born on the street,
and back there again.

47:59.979 --> 48:05.652
That's why I want to find her
a home full of love!

48:05.818 --> 48:10.240
All I ever wanted was love!

48:17.372 --> 48:18.248
Ow!

48:24.879 --> 48:26.756
What the hell?!

48:29.384 --> 48:31.886
The geezer's come out.

48:32.095 --> 48:33.429
Where are my clothes?!

48:43.273 --> 48:45.108
Way to go, Gin!

48:46.901 --> 48:49.112
Come back any time.

48:50.238 --> 48:52.657
Thank you, Mother.

48:55.702 --> 49:02.250
My mother's white breath / as she
watches me set out / on a long journey.

50:17.992 --> 50:20.411
Oh, man!

50:20.787 --> 50:24.332
An empty building's always nice,
but look who got here first.

50:27.877 --> 50:31.422
L'd just love to fill up
on some meat!

50:32.048 --> 50:33.883
Don't you dare!

50:35.552 --> 50:38.054
Just kidding!

50:42.725 --> 50:46.229
The snow's let up.
Miyuki, will you go shopping?

50:46.396 --> 50:47.397
Okay.

50:47.564 --> 50:49.774
Get me some sake.

50:50.400 --> 50:52.110
Just one.

51:10.128 --> 51:12.422
- No!
- I wish.

51:29.606 --> 51:30.940
"Honey, I'm home."

51:48.875 --> 51:54.881
You stayed in there?
You'd think you were homeless!

51:59.344 --> 52:02.680
Actually, we're looking for
these people.

52:04.182 --> 52:06.434
Sachiko Nishizawa.

52:06.893 --> 52:08.144
Do you know her?

52:08.645 --> 52:12.357
She never paid me back for her
Neighborhood Association dues.

52:12.524 --> 52:14.859
Are you a relative?

52:15.026 --> 52:19.572
No! We're acquaintances
of a relative.

52:19.948 --> 52:22.158
Her husband was no better.

52:22.325 --> 52:26.788
Gambling day and night,
and mean when he drank.

52:28.831 --> 52:31.960
Living on his wife's earnings
and borrowed money.

52:32.168 --> 52:33.920
Where are they now?

52:34.087 --> 52:37.715
I wouldn't know.
Mrs. Kurumizawa might.

52:38.258 --> 52:41.719
They left
about three months ago.

52:42.679 --> 52:49.185
The house was seized for debt.
One night they just up and went.

52:50.019 --> 52:53.147
They were a nice couple
at first...

52:53.356 --> 52:57.277
...but it wasn't long before
they started fighting.

52:57.443 --> 52:59.445
That's poverty for you.

52:59.612 --> 53:03.908
All that debt didn't stop him
from lording it over her.

53:04.075 --> 53:07.662
Even the most dedicated wife
has her limits.

53:08.788 --> 53:10.832
You'd see bruises sometimes.

53:11.040 --> 53:12.792
The poor woman.

53:12.959 --> 53:15.503
Not on her, on him!

53:15.712 --> 53:16.880
Oh, dear!

53:17.589 --> 53:24.345
But his mother would always take
his side against her.

53:25.430 --> 53:28.224
His parents built them this house.

53:28.391 --> 53:30.310
Where do they live?

53:30.476 --> 53:32.729
Mrs. Yamanouchi might know.

53:34.898 --> 53:37.192
Her mother-in-law
was always complaining...

53:37.400 --> 53:39.527
...that she never did
any housework.

53:39.736 --> 53:41.946
But her son was perfect,
of course.

53:42.113 --> 53:44.782
Of course!
That's why I told her...

53:44.949 --> 53:49.037
...she'd never see a grandchild
with his wife working in a club.

53:49.579 --> 53:52.373
But she did get pregnant.

53:52.582 --> 53:54.834
Well, a man and a woman...

53:55.001 --> 53:56.586
They can always find time...

53:56.753 --> 53:58.880
...to do what they must!

53:59.088 --> 54:02.550
Shinkocho 1-2-25
Maison Happiness Apt. 203

54:03.843 --> 54:06.179
What if they ran out
from this new place too?

54:06.346 --> 54:08.765
What a horrible man!

54:09.015 --> 54:14.229
Poor Sachiko! Working to pay off
her husband's gambling debts!

54:14.437 --> 54:15.647
Right!

54:15.980 --> 54:20.443
But I never thought of
abandoning the kid!

54:20.818 --> 54:22.987
- Huh?
- Nothing.

54:23.154 --> 54:27.242
That's no reason
to just dump the kid!

54:27.450 --> 54:29.077
L've said that all along.

54:32.247 --> 54:36.626
Miyuki: Angel has
come home. Dad.

54:41.130 --> 54:44.050
Doesn't it ever get tired
of snowing?

54:46.553 --> 54:48.471
Thank you.

54:58.064 --> 55:01.484
I wonder how we look
to them.

55:01.651 --> 55:04.320
Like a bum, a homo,
a runaway and a foundling.

55:04.821 --> 55:08.283
Kiyoko is God's messenger.
We're her servants.

55:09.492 --> 55:11.828
Unpaid servants.

55:12.120 --> 55:15.248
Paying for a father's sins.

55:15.415 --> 55:18.626
Yeah, if her father had been
any good at all...

55:18.835 --> 55:21.171
...we wouldn't be going
through all this.

55:22.839 --> 55:27.969
Even a good-for-nothing father
never forgets a child.

55:30.054 --> 55:31.556
I'm going out.

55:36.019 --> 55:38.688
What's the matter with her?

55:38.855 --> 55:42.358
A child never forgets
its parents.

55:47.030 --> 55:50.033
I never stop wanting...

55:51.201 --> 55:53.828
...to see my daughter, just once.

55:54.037 --> 55:56.080
So she's alive?

55:56.456 --> 55:57.624
Yeah.

55:57.790 --> 55:58.958
And your wife?

56:00.251 --> 56:02.462
I'm sure she's remarried...

56:03.046 --> 56:05.340
...and living happily.

56:10.345 --> 56:11.429
"Hello.

56:11.971 --> 56:13.598
It's me, Miyuki."

56:14.349 --> 56:16.309
Why did you split up?

56:16.559 --> 56:18.645
- Drinking and gambling.
- What?!

56:19.896 --> 56:21.231
Just like...

56:22.315 --> 56:24.609
I'm a louse.

56:25.735 --> 56:30.865
But I've always wanted to do
something for her as a father...

56:31.115 --> 56:32.617
...even just a little.

56:33.493 --> 56:37.121
When I was gambling
this would have been nothing.

56:37.539 --> 56:41.042
Now I've had to sweat blood
just to save 30,000 yen.

56:41.251 --> 56:43.378
That's great, Gin!

56:43.753 --> 56:45.380
We can stuff ourselves!

56:45.588 --> 56:47.090
Stuff you!

56:56.808 --> 56:58.142
Ishida speaking.

57:06.943 --> 57:10.071
Miyuki? Is that you?

57:12.407 --> 57:13.575
Are you all right?

57:19.581 --> 57:21.040
I'm sorry!

57:21.207 --> 57:22.834
I'm sorry!

57:23.459 --> 57:25.253
I'm sorry!

57:27.463 --> 57:29.966
Excuse me,
but if you wouldn't mind...

57:30.133 --> 57:31.759
"Get out", you mean?

57:32.135 --> 57:35.638
Other customers
might like to sit down.

57:35.889 --> 57:37.307
There's hardly anyone here!

57:37.473 --> 57:39.100
You guys stink!

57:39.851 --> 57:43.438
What are you?
Homeless or something?

57:44.063 --> 57:48.109
Does trash have kids too?
Just like real people?

57:48.818 --> 57:50.945
Who are you looking at?

57:53.156 --> 57:54.449
Hold it, you!

57:55.325 --> 57:56.826
Sir! No!

57:56.993 --> 57:58.995
Hold it, I said, you low-life!

58:09.047 --> 58:12.509
It's New Year's Sale time
at The Food Store!

58:12.842 --> 58:19.224
Come to The Food Store
for all your special New Year's needs!

58:19.390 --> 58:22.060
See in the New Year
with your family!

58:22.227 --> 58:24.020
Call an ambulance, quick.

58:24.771 --> 58:26.147
Right!

58:29.359 --> 58:34.072
I knew it! Kiyoko really is
the messenger of God!

58:36.699 --> 58:37.033
Hey!

58:38.034 --> 58:38.535
Miss Hana!

58:38.701 --> 58:40.119
Hey!

58:40.286 --> 58:41.329
Hana!

58:57.720 --> 59:00.431
Following a recent
gangland shooting incident...

59:00.598 --> 59:06.187
...police are seeking a fugitive
thought to be Latin American.

59:06.813 --> 59:09.524
Mitsuo Hiruta, shot three times...

59:09.691 --> 59:13.528
...in protecting the leader
of his syndicate...

59:13.820 --> 59:19.075
...will be questioned after he recovers
from his wounds.

59:19.951 --> 59:23.538
Isn't she cute!
When was she born?

59:23.746 --> 59:26.708
Not long ago, I guess.

59:27.125 --> 59:28.626
So the mother...

59:28.793 --> 59:30.378
I'm not.

59:30.920 --> 59:32.714
What's her name?

59:32.881 --> 59:33.298
Kiyoko.

59:33.464 --> 59:37.385
That's my name too.
What a coincidence.

59:40.096 --> 59:42.390
Your friend is very weak.

59:42.599 --> 59:45.476
Make sure he gets rest
and proper nutrition.

59:45.643 --> 59:46.895
Doctor!

59:47.770 --> 59:50.231
Believe it or not,
we're homeless.

59:50.398 --> 59:52.609
I'm just a doctor.

59:54.027 --> 59:59.574
Rest and nutrition don't fit
with our lifestyle, you realize.

01:00:00.533 --> 01:00:06.623
I can try to cure disease.
Lifestyle is something you have to fix.

01:00:06.789 --> 01:00:10.084
All anyone can do is their best.

01:00:12.462 --> 01:00:14.255
Take care.

01:00:17.800 --> 01:00:20.929
The bill for today is 29,830 yen.

01:00:21.137 --> 01:00:25.308
Bring your health-insurance card
and you'll get a refund.

01:00:26.476 --> 01:00:28.937
I'm sorry, Gin!

01:00:29.687 --> 01:00:33.274
Stop crying! You'll get
the bills all wet.

01:00:33.983 --> 01:00:35.985
That's 30,000 yen.

01:00:52.252 --> 01:00:53.545
Kiyoko?!

01:00:58.591 --> 01:00:59.634
Dad?

01:01:22.574 --> 01:01:24.659
So you took up nursing.

01:01:25.952 --> 01:01:28.162
I see.

01:01:30.540 --> 01:01:32.417
I'm glad you're well.

01:01:32.584 --> 01:01:38.006
Oh, yeah, I'm just great.
How's your mother?

01:01:38.214 --> 01:01:39.424
Fine.

01:01:40.341 --> 01:01:42.510
Yeah? That's good.

01:01:43.136 --> 01:01:44.846
What are you doing now?

01:01:45.013 --> 01:01:51.269
I'm in recycling.
I had to drop something off here.

01:01:55.315 --> 01:01:57.025
You must hate me.

01:01:58.610 --> 01:02:02.572
I was never any kind
of a father to you.

01:02:02.989 --> 01:02:08.870
But that 30,000 yen was money
I'd saved up for you.

01:02:10.413 --> 01:02:11.873
You may not believe it.

01:02:15.293 --> 01:02:18.546
I always wanted to see you.

01:02:19.839 --> 01:02:23.968
When I was little,
Mom and I searched for you.

01:02:24.260 --> 01:02:26.888
We even checked
unidentified corpses.

01:02:27.847 --> 01:02:32.227
After you disappeared,
Mom ran the store herself.

01:02:33.686 --> 01:02:34.437
The store?

01:02:34.604 --> 01:02:38.775
It was hard for a woman to run
a bicycle shop alone.

01:02:39.776 --> 01:02:42.779
That's not quite the same as
a bicycle racer.

01:02:43.029 --> 01:02:49.160
The man you owed money to was shot
and wounded the other day, you know.

01:02:49.327 --> 01:02:50.745
He lived?!

01:02:51.788 --> 01:02:53.831
That's a relief.

01:02:53.998 --> 01:02:55.959
I thought you'd say that.

01:02:58.837 --> 01:03:03.758
I ran up the debts, not him.

01:03:05.385 --> 01:03:09.931
Thank that doctor for me.
He seems like a nice guy.

01:03:10.849 --> 01:03:13.268
I'm getting married.

01:03:15.144 --> 01:03:16.855
Oh? That's good.

01:03:17.021 --> 01:03:18.273
To him.

01:03:18.439 --> 01:03:22.861
Great! But isn't he
about my age?

01:03:23.528 --> 01:03:27.282
He's been married.
His daughter got sick and died...

01:03:27.824 --> 01:03:30.118
...and his wife followed her.

01:03:35.373 --> 01:03:37.125
That man makes me so mad!

01:03:37.333 --> 01:03:38.918
Aren't you moved?

01:03:39.836 --> 01:03:42.630
Here's the address
and phone number.

01:03:42.797 --> 01:03:43.715
Yours?

01:03:43.882 --> 01:03:46.301
The old house is gone.

01:03:46.467 --> 01:03:48.845
Even if you can't now,
call me sometime.

01:03:50.054 --> 01:03:52.390
Kiyoko!

01:03:54.434 --> 01:03:58.521
L've had about
all I can stand!

01:03:58.688 --> 01:03:59.480
Miss Hana?

01:03:59.689 --> 01:04:02.358
Telling us you were a racer!

01:04:03.359 --> 01:04:05.361
I was always at the track.

01:04:05.528 --> 01:04:06.863
Yeah, betting!

01:04:07.030 --> 01:04:11.326
And your debts snowballed
so you couldn't face your family...

01:04:11.492 --> 01:04:13.369
...and you ran and hid
in a cardboard box!

01:04:13.536 --> 01:04:15.246
Yes, damn it!

01:04:15.413 --> 01:04:17.874
That's what your father is!

01:04:18.374 --> 01:04:22.003
He can't bet, he's spineless,
his feet stink and he can't drink!

01:04:22.212 --> 01:04:26.049
He kills off his wife and daughter
to buy sympathy!

01:04:26.216 --> 01:04:29.052
He said you had
an incurable disease!

01:04:29.219 --> 01:04:34.390
With a father like that,
you have my sympathy!

01:04:34.724 --> 01:04:37.685
Is this how you repay me?!

01:04:38.061 --> 01:04:39.771
Repay you?!

01:04:39.938 --> 01:04:41.856
Am I hearing right?

01:04:42.065 --> 01:04:44.192
If we're talking about debt,
I'm waiting for my change!

01:04:44.400 --> 01:04:46.861
Debt's a concept
you don't even understand!

01:04:47.070 --> 01:04:50.532
You understand how to troll
through garbage cans!

01:04:50.740 --> 01:04:53.576
And how to get in debt
and how to make babies.

01:04:53.743 --> 01:04:57.288
Though you're not too good
at raising them, are you?

01:04:57.455 --> 01:05:00.375
And your debts
you shove off on your wife.

01:05:00.542 --> 01:05:03.920
Always running away,
never doing anything right!

01:05:04.087 --> 01:05:06.798
Running away's
the only racing you ever did!

01:05:06.965 --> 01:05:10.051
Miyuki! We're leaving!

01:05:12.929 --> 01:05:14.055
Miss Hana?

01:05:19.602 --> 01:05:21.604
I guess he's better.

01:05:22.939 --> 01:05:25.984
Should you have said that
in front of her?

01:05:28.778 --> 01:05:32.073
If she's his daughter,
she'll forgive him.

01:05:34.993 --> 01:05:38.246
Being able to speak freely...

01:05:38.413 --> 01:05:41.249
...is the lifeblood of love.

01:05:42.292 --> 01:05:43.793
Maybe I'm naive.

01:05:46.671 --> 01:05:49.007
So you're in love with him?

01:05:49.174 --> 01:05:52.635
Don't be silly.
I'm the Weeping Red Devil.

01:05:52.802 --> 01:05:53.469
What?

01:05:54.137 --> 01:05:56.848
It's a story I love.

01:05:57.515 --> 01:06:02.353
There was a red devil who
wanted to be friends with people.

01:06:03.313 --> 01:06:08.026
But since he was a devil,
no one would go near him.

01:06:08.193 --> 01:06:11.863
So his friend the blue devil
made a plan.

01:06:12.989 --> 01:06:18.494
He'd wreak havoc among the people,
and the red devil would save them.

01:06:24.167 --> 01:06:27.295
When you try to achieve something,
someone's bound to get hurt.

01:06:28.338 --> 01:06:30.673
You always have to
sacrifice something.

01:06:31.508 --> 01:06:33.635
The plan worked.

01:06:33.843 --> 01:06:38.723
But the blue devil had to go away
so they'd never know it was a trick.

01:06:41.559 --> 01:06:43.144
It's a sad story.

01:06:43.353 --> 01:06:47.524
But that means you leave.
Where will you go?

01:06:48.525 --> 01:06:51.861
It's best for everyone
when they're with their family.

01:06:52.028 --> 01:06:54.030
Soon we'll find Kiyoko's mother.

01:06:54.197 --> 01:06:58.535
And then what?
You don't have a real family!

01:07:08.545 --> 01:07:11.881
Rare "Line Of Ones" Wins Lottery

01:07:12.048 --> 01:07:16.678
Numbers have been drawn for the
annual New Year's Jumbo Lottery.

01:07:17.220 --> 01:07:20.640
Top prize in the 200-million-yen
lottery is a very rare number.

01:07:21.391 --> 01:07:25.520
Group 11, number 111, 111...

01:07:25.770 --> 01:07:28.439
...is worth 50 million yen.

01:07:29.107 --> 01:07:30.400
A different group pays 100,000 yen.

01:07:31.526 --> 01:07:34.863
To repeat,
the winning prize number is...

01:07:36.739 --> 01:07:38.366
This just in.

01:07:38.825 --> 01:07:42.412
Police have released a sketch
of an infant taken...

01:07:42.579 --> 01:07:46.374
...from a hospital in
Tokyo's Shinagawa Ward.

01:07:48.751 --> 01:07:53.715
We've come all the way here,
but we don't have her address!

01:07:53.882 --> 01:07:56.426
The geezer's got it!
Let's go back.

01:07:56.593 --> 01:07:58.928
Where are you going?

01:08:00.513 --> 01:08:04.726
- The police!
- What? You hated that idea!

01:08:05.643 --> 01:08:07.604
I was just ego-tripping.

01:08:08.354 --> 01:08:11.566
Now I want to apologize
to her parents.

01:08:11.774 --> 01:08:16.070
They might not be able to sleep
waiting for news about her.

01:08:16.279 --> 01:08:19.908
That's what we said
from the very start!

01:08:20.116 --> 01:08:24.245
They might even be
about to commit suicide!

01:08:24.412 --> 01:08:27.916
L've done something
that can't be taken back!

01:08:28.124 --> 01:08:30.585
I'll throw myself in this river.

01:08:30.793 --> 01:08:34.923
I'll step neatly out of my shoes, stand
on the handrail, and be at peace.

01:08:35.131 --> 01:08:38.134
But then I'll see
a baby's face on the water.

01:08:38.301 --> 01:08:43.014
No! While I see this child's face,
I cannot die!

01:08:43.181 --> 01:08:44.933
Hey, you!

01:08:45.141 --> 01:08:46.351
No!

01:08:48.686 --> 01:08:49.812
You're too young for this!

01:08:49.979 --> 01:08:52.106
Please! Let me die!

01:08:59.739 --> 01:09:01.282
You!

01:09:02.075 --> 01:09:03.284
Sachiko Nishizawa.

01:09:07.830 --> 01:09:09.791
What were you thinking of?!

01:09:09.999 --> 01:09:12.001
Is that an apology?

01:09:12.168 --> 01:09:16.297
If we hadn't found this child,
she would've frozen to death!

01:09:16.506 --> 01:09:17.799
It wasn't me!

01:09:18.007 --> 01:09:21.177
My husband took her away
when I wasn't there!

01:09:22.345 --> 01:09:25.139
L've looked and looked!

01:09:32.355 --> 01:09:33.523
Is that true?

01:09:36.693 --> 01:09:41.865
All I've suffered
on account of that man!

01:09:53.168 --> 01:09:56.045
"Hi, Mom!"

01:10:04.095 --> 01:10:07.682
God really loves this child,
you know.

01:10:08.057 --> 01:10:11.186
I want you to give her
lots of love too.

01:10:11.603 --> 01:10:14.522
Do right by her,
or you'll pay for it.

01:10:14.689 --> 01:10:16.524
I'm so sorry!

01:10:16.733 --> 01:10:17.942
I'm sorry!

01:10:27.952 --> 01:10:29.579
Mrs. Nishizawa!

01:11:16.125 --> 01:11:17.252
What are you doing in here?!

01:11:17.460 --> 01:11:19.754
Get out of here! Get out!

01:11:20.338 --> 01:11:22.298
Wait! I'm no thief.

01:11:22.465 --> 01:11:24.801
You're lying! Get out!

01:11:24.968 --> 01:11:26.094
Where's the baby?!

01:11:29.639 --> 01:11:32.809
Did an old queer and a girl
come to give it back?

01:11:32.976 --> 01:11:34.519
What are you talking about?!

01:11:34.686 --> 01:11:36.813
You abandoned a baby!

01:11:39.023 --> 01:11:41.109
I can prove it.

01:11:41.568 --> 01:11:43.653
Are you a cop?

01:11:43.820 --> 01:11:48.449
Huh? I'm just a bum
who was passing by.

01:11:49.659 --> 01:11:51.619
Are you right in the head?

01:11:51.828 --> 01:11:53.955
I'm damn near crazy
from all this!

01:11:54.330 --> 01:11:59.460
Why is the baby you abandoned
on the news as being "taken away"?

01:11:59.669 --> 01:12:02.130
They'll call us kidnappers!

01:12:02.672 --> 01:12:06.759
It wasn't me.
That's not my kid.

01:12:09.345 --> 01:12:10.305
What?

01:12:12.182 --> 01:12:14.392
There, there! Don't cry!

01:12:14.559 --> 01:12:15.643
Take care.

01:12:16.352 --> 01:12:17.979
Raise her right.

01:12:18.146 --> 01:12:20.231
See you again someday.

01:12:21.858 --> 01:12:24.485
Never leave her again.

01:12:47.383 --> 01:12:54.891
On the year's last day / when all of a
life's accounts / have been settled up.

01:13:05.068 --> 01:13:09.864
Sachiko stole that baby
out of the hospital.

01:13:10.073 --> 01:13:14.285
She stole a baby
and then abandoned it?!

01:13:14.452 --> 01:13:16.371
That's a person's life!

01:13:16.538 --> 01:13:19.123
She lied to me about it!

01:13:19.290 --> 01:13:22.544
And now it's gone
way out of control.

01:13:22.919 --> 01:13:27.382
I don't want anything to do with it!
Take the kid to the police!

01:13:27.549 --> 01:13:28.967
What?!

01:13:30.093 --> 01:13:32.887
Don't act like
you're not part of this!

01:13:33.096 --> 01:13:36.224
You don't want to get involved?
You're her husband!

01:13:36.641 --> 01:13:40.770
That's all over!
I'm getting my life back together.

01:13:41.020 --> 01:13:41.729
Look!

01:13:41.938 --> 01:13:45.733
I won 100,000 yen in the lottery.
My luck's turned!

01:13:49.279 --> 01:13:55.243
I know a guy just like you.
He threw away his life and his family.

01:13:55.618 --> 01:13:57.745
No. They threw him away.

01:13:57.996 --> 01:13:59.998
I'm no loser!

01:14:04.878 --> 01:14:07.088
These were in your wife's bag.

01:14:09.465 --> 01:14:12.760
Any idea where
she might have gone?

01:14:13.011 --> 01:14:16.264
She said she was going
to be with her baby.

01:14:16.806 --> 01:14:19.601
She was going to kill herself!

01:14:21.477 --> 01:14:23.104
There's no time to waste!

01:14:23.271 --> 01:14:26.816
No! She was just going
to go look for the kid.

01:14:26.983 --> 01:14:29.444
She's desperate.
That only means one thing!

01:14:31.154 --> 01:14:32.614
But where do I look?!

01:14:48.796 --> 01:14:49.797
Hana!

01:14:50.006 --> 01:14:51.299
Miyuki!

01:14:53.009 --> 01:14:54.302
Kiyoko!

01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:03.144
God must be busy
at this time of year.

01:15:03.353 --> 01:15:05.647
Better once a year than never.

01:15:06.564 --> 01:15:07.273
Geezer?

01:15:16.866 --> 01:15:20.828
You're too late. You just missed
a very moving finale.

01:15:21.037 --> 01:15:22.956
What's the matter?

01:15:26.709 --> 01:15:27.710
"Kiyoko"!

01:15:31.214 --> 01:15:32.090
"Stomach"?

01:15:34.425 --> 01:15:35.510
"Mother"!

01:15:35.718 --> 01:15:37.220
Now that's settled...

01:15:37.387 --> 01:15:39.097
...what the hell do you mean?!

01:15:39.556 --> 01:15:43.434
Fake! The mother!
Sachiko's a fake!

01:15:45.645 --> 01:15:46.688
Pardon?

01:15:52.318 --> 01:15:54.863
Why won't you drink?

01:15:55.613 --> 01:16:00.076
A baby has to drink
from its mother's breast.

01:16:00.702 --> 01:16:04.789
We'll never be close
if you don't!

01:16:11.254 --> 01:16:12.922
Sorry. Wrong people.

01:16:15.466 --> 01:16:17.427
She can't be far!

01:16:17.886 --> 01:16:19.804
But where do we look?

01:16:19.971 --> 01:16:22.599
We can't just give her up now!

01:16:35.570 --> 01:16:37.071
That's Kiyoko!

01:16:44.287 --> 01:16:45.872
Should you be running?

01:16:46.039 --> 01:16:48.625
If I don't run now, when will I?

01:16:49.042 --> 01:16:49.918
This way!

01:17:04.224 --> 01:17:08.144
Returning stolen goods to a thief!
How could we be so dumb?!

01:17:08.311 --> 01:17:10.063
Who said "family suicide"?

01:17:10.230 --> 01:17:11.689
You did!

01:17:17.820 --> 01:17:18.780
- Which way?
- Left.

01:17:18.988 --> 01:17:20.990
- Okay, right!
- Why?

01:17:21.491 --> 01:17:22.742
You're a lousy gambler!

01:17:22.909 --> 01:17:24.994
You got that right.

01:17:25.161 --> 01:17:27.038
Somebody help!

01:17:40.677 --> 01:17:41.928
Hey!

01:17:42.428 --> 01:17:43.304
Wait!

01:17:43.513 --> 01:17:45.139
Thief! Thief!

01:17:45.348 --> 01:17:45.974
What's wrong?

01:17:46.182 --> 01:17:49.727
A woman just stole my truck!

01:17:50.436 --> 01:17:51.688
Hey! Thief!

01:17:51.855 --> 01:17:53.982
Yes! That woman!

01:17:54.482 --> 01:17:57.277
She's a baby thief!

01:18:11.749 --> 01:18:15.086
Be quiet, will you?
Please! Be a good baby!

01:18:23.469 --> 01:18:25.722
Stop! Give Kiyoko back!

01:18:30.310 --> 01:18:31.978
Give me a break!

01:18:32.145 --> 01:18:34.189
I'm forever in your debt!

01:18:39.402 --> 01:18:40.403
Gin!

01:18:42.113 --> 01:18:44.240
That woman's crazy!

01:18:44.782 --> 01:18:45.617
Get closer!

01:18:45.783 --> 01:18:46.576
I can't!

01:18:46.743 --> 01:18:49.037
You have to, for Kiyoko!

01:18:49.245 --> 01:18:51.039
- Who's Kiyoko?!
- Step on it like a man!

01:18:51.247 --> 01:18:52.373
Okay!

01:18:57.253 --> 01:18:59.839
Please! Be quiet!

01:19:03.551 --> 01:19:05.094
- Gin!
- Geezer?!

01:19:08.723 --> 01:19:09.390
Geezer!

01:19:09.599 --> 01:19:13.061
Go for it, Gin!
No action star can touch you!

01:19:13.353 --> 01:19:14.812
Pass her!

01:19:14.979 --> 01:19:15.772
We'll die!

01:19:15.939 --> 01:19:16.689
Step on it!

01:19:16.856 --> 01:19:18.525
Okay!

01:19:20.276 --> 01:19:21.945
Stop crying!

01:19:22.820 --> 01:19:25.907
Don't be afraid.
I'll never leave you again.

01:19:26.449 --> 01:19:27.492
You want to die?!

01:19:36.709 --> 01:19:38.628
Gin!

01:19:50.682 --> 01:19:52.016
Gin!

01:19:54.561 --> 01:19:55.603
There!

01:19:57.313 --> 01:19:58.898
- Are you okay?!
- Where's Kiyoko?

01:19:59.065 --> 01:20:00.650
- Faster!
- Okay!

01:20:20.336 --> 01:20:20.837
Which way?

01:21:08.176 --> 01:21:09.844
We're at the scene...

01:21:10.053 --> 01:21:14.516
...where a truck has crashed
into a building in Shinagawa.

01:21:14.724 --> 01:21:18.978
Now a woman holding a baby
has appeared on the roof.

01:21:19.479 --> 01:21:24.192
Witnesses say the woman
is connected with the incident...

01:21:24.400 --> 01:21:26.653
...as she was driving the truck.

01:21:32.909 --> 01:21:35.703
Now there's someone else
on the roof!

01:21:40.416 --> 01:21:41.292
Stay away!

01:21:41.459 --> 01:21:43.628
No!

01:21:50.468 --> 01:21:52.929
Tell me why you took
that baby.

01:21:53.096 --> 01:21:53.805
I didn't!

01:21:54.097 --> 01:21:56.516
This baby is mine!

01:21:56.683 --> 01:22:00.228
You're lying! Its real parents
are worried sick about it!

01:22:00.436 --> 01:22:01.563
That's not true!

01:22:01.771 --> 01:22:05.692
You of all people should know
what it's like to lose a child!

01:22:17.203 --> 01:22:22.458
She's dead. My baby died
before she was even born!

01:22:29.883 --> 01:22:33.636
All the other babies
looked so healthy there in the ward.

01:22:33.803 --> 01:22:36.306
I wanted to die.

01:22:36.472 --> 01:22:39.058
But then this baby
smiled at me.

01:22:39.225 --> 01:22:41.269
I decided she was mine.

01:22:41.477 --> 01:22:45.565
I thought as long as I had her,
everything would be fine.

01:22:45.732 --> 01:22:49.402
My husband would mend his ways,
and we'd be a real family.

01:22:49.569 --> 01:22:51.362
That's bullshit!

01:22:51.738 --> 01:22:56.993
Build a family by ruining a baby's life?
If you're going to die, do it alone!

01:22:57.160 --> 01:23:01.998
A life is a life. It's only born once.
You, me, or Kiyoko.

01:23:07.545 --> 01:23:09.589
Give her back, okay?

01:23:16.930 --> 01:23:18.848
I want to be reborn.

01:23:19.849 --> 01:23:21.935
Sachiko!

01:23:23.186 --> 01:23:26.189
Sachiko, don't die!
Come back to me!

01:23:26.356 --> 01:23:30.193
I was wrong!
Please, don't kill yourself!

01:23:30.610 --> 01:23:33.196
We'll start again!
We'll be reborn!

01:23:33.530 --> 01:23:35.156
Sachiko!

01:23:35.365 --> 01:23:38.159
I'll go first and wait for you.

01:23:42.539 --> 01:23:43.665
Sachiko!

01:23:46.125 --> 01:23:47.377
Please! Let me die!

01:23:47.544 --> 01:23:50.630
Kiyoko wants to see
her mom and dad!

01:23:56.594 --> 01:23:58.054
I want to go home.

01:24:01.349 --> 01:24:03.685
I'm sorry!

01:24:11.359 --> 01:24:12.277
Take her...

01:24:12.902 --> 01:24:15.530
...to her mother and father.

01:24:24.998 --> 01:24:25.748
Oh, no.

01:24:26.749 --> 01:24:28.084
Hana!

01:24:29.752 --> 01:24:30.920
I'm okay!

01:24:31.504 --> 01:24:32.922
I'm still alive!

01:25:13.546 --> 01:25:17.550
Inspector, I don't know
how to thank you.

01:25:17.717 --> 01:25:21.387
We're not the ones
you should thank.

01:25:23.556 --> 01:25:28.561
Man, that was a good sleep!
Get me a cigarette, Miyuki.

01:25:28.728 --> 01:25:30.980
- In my jacket.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:31.147 --> 01:25:34.400
That was some New Year's!

01:25:35.235 --> 01:25:36.986
It's "No Smoking" here.

01:25:37.195 --> 01:25:40.281
Lighten up! I'm a hero!

01:25:40.490 --> 01:25:42.617
You mean "we"!

01:25:46.079 --> 01:25:51.376
I guess we won't have to listen to
Kiyoko's damn crying anymore.

01:25:51.543 --> 01:25:53.753
She's not "Kiyoko" anymore.

01:25:53.920 --> 01:25:56.256
I'm not pleased.

01:25:57.173 --> 01:25:58.967
What can we do?

01:25:59.175 --> 01:26:00.802
Not that.

01:26:01.344 --> 01:26:03.513
This is a men's ward!

01:26:06.349 --> 01:26:07.934
Perhaps we're intruding.

01:26:08.101 --> 01:26:10.311
No, it's just...

01:26:10.854 --> 01:26:13.273
...I'm told they're homeless.

01:26:13.439 --> 01:26:14.649
Who cares?

01:26:14.858 --> 01:26:17.735
We'd like them to be
her godfathers.

01:26:19.529 --> 01:26:20.530
Come in.

01:26:21.739 --> 01:26:22.740
Excuse us.

01:26:23.533 --> 01:26:26.953
The baby's parents
would like to thank you

01:26:32.625 --> 01:26:34.002
Dad...
